 "notes": "Curve traced from the vector fill polygons of Fig. 4 in the arXiv e-print (figure4.pdf): combined lower envelope of the two new 95% CL limits, Yb+E3/E2 (salmon, dominant below ~1e-21 eV) and Yb+E3/Sr (blue, ~3x stronger above ~1e-20 eV). Axes calibrated from tick/grid strokes (x: 1e-23..1e-17 eV, y: 1e-10..1e-4) and cross-checked against the top frequency axis (1e-5 Hz -> 4.14e-20 eV). Noisy periodogram-derived boundary downsampled to per-log-bin medians (91 points). Limits include the factor-3 stochastic-field rescaling of Centers et al. as stated in the paper, and assume rho_DM = 0.4 GeV/cm^3 (Eq. 8). Physics cross-check via Eq. 8 with A~7e-18, k_alpha~6 reproduces d_e~2e-7 at 4e-20 eV, consistent with the extracted curve. Mass range restricted to the plotted range (1.5e-23 to 2.1e-17 eV) although the text quotes sensitivity down to ~1e-24 eV.",
